# Line endings.
#
# These files are read by Linux inside the containers, where a CRLF is not
# whitespace but part of the token. A checkout on Windows converts endings by
# default (core.autocrlf=true), and `docker-entrypoint.sh` with a CRLF shebang
# fails at container start as:
#
#   exec ./docker-entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# which names the file it just found, and so reads as anything but a line
# ending problem. Pin them to LF in the working tree as well as in the repo.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf
